    "description": "At AMD, we believe technology has the power to solve the world&rsquo;s most important challenges. From advancing healthcare and scientific discovery to powering AI and the technologies people rely on every day, innovation at AMD is shaping the future.\n\nWhether you&rsquo;re designing next-gen processors, enabling AI breakthroughs, or bringing leading edge products to market, every role at AMD contributes to something bigger — technology that moves the world forward. Join us and, together, we&rsquo;ll advance your career.\n\nThe Enterprise AI Business Development team is seeking a highly motivated early-career professional to support a broad range of business operations activities within one of the company&rsquo;s fastest-growing areas. This is an ideal opportunity for a recent college graduate who enjoys solving problems, is highly organized, and is eager to learn how a technology business operates from the inside.\n\nIn this role, you will gain exposure to multiple aspects of the Enterprise AI business, including customer engagement support, product sample management, supply and demand tracking, business planning, operational execution, reporting, and cross-functional coordination.\n\nYou will work closely with business development, product management, sales, operations, engineering, marketing, and finance teams to help drive operational excellence across a wide range of strategic initiatives. Prior AI industry experience is not required.\n\nYou are intellectually curious, highly organized, and eager to take ownership of new challenges. You thrive in a fast-paced, constantly evolving environment and are willing to roll up your sleeves to help the team succeed.\n\nYou are dependable, responsive, and committed to following tasks through to completion. You enjoy solving problems, improving processes, and learning every aspect of how a business operates. You bring a strong work ethic, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while collaborating effectively across diverse teams and functions.\n\nThis position provides a unique opportunity to gain broad exposure across multiple functions within a high-growth Enterprise AI business. You will receive hands-on experience working with senior leaders, supporting strategic initiatives, and developing the operational, analytical, and business skills needed for long-term career growth.\n\nThis role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.\n\nBenefits offered are described: AMD benefits at a glance .\n\nAMD does not accept unsolicited resumes from headhunters, recruitment agencies, or fee-based recruitment services. AMD and its subsidiaries are equal opportunity, inclusive employers and will consider all applicants without regard to age, ancestry, color, marital status, medical condition, mental or physical disability, national origin, race, religion, political and/or third-party affiliation, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. We encourage applications from all qualified candidates and will accommodate applicants&rsquo; needs under the respective laws throughout all stages of the recruitment and selection process.\n\nAMD may use Artificial Intelligence to help screen, assess or select applicants for this position. AMD&rsquo;s &ldquo;Responsible AI Policy&rdquo; is available here.\n\nThis posting is for an existing vacancy.",
